# `precommit` runs `lint-staged --no-stash`. The default backup stash races the Quimby agent-clone
# working-tree capture (both git-stash the same tree), which could inject conflict markers into staged
# files — so agents had to commit `--no-verify`, losing commit-msg validation. `--no-stash` removes that
# stash; lint-staged still bounds work to staged files ∩ globs. The only cost is partial-stage handling
# (`git add -p`), which this codebase's whole-file staging does not use. Do not drop `--no-stash`.
npm run precommit
